1781 0 obj
<<
/Title (Expected comparison: translation-only has the fewest complex warping artifacts but looks less realistic. Per-object affine is a practical compromise for a two-wheeler. Keypoint-based motion can look more natural but may create flicker and uncovered road/track regions. Choose the simplest model that gives acceptable continuity and does not misrepresent the incident. Safeguards: obtain permission before animating identifiable people; blur faces and vehicle registration plates unless explicit consent and legal approval exist; do not fabricate an event and label it as real evidence. Modern first-order motion models transfer learned keypoint motion from a driving video. Diffusion video models generate plausible frames from text or image conditioning. Both can create convincing deepfakes, so provenance labels, consent and clear disclosure are essential.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1763 0 R
/Prev 1807 0 R
>>
endobj
